<title>Λήψη ειδοποιήσεων νέων μηνυμάτων</title>

<p><app>Evolution</app> always notifies you of new messages by adding a small emblem to the mailer icon in the window <link xref="intro-main-window">switcher</link>.</p>
<media type="image" src="./figures/new-mail-switcher.png" width="256" its:locNote="Translators: Please make sure that the screenshot does have the small yellow star in the Mail icon">
  <p>Διάταξη εναλλάκτη όταν ένα νέο μήνυμα φτάνει</p>
</media>

<p>In order to also be notified of new messages in GNOME desktop notifications:</p>
<steps>
<item><p>Επιλέξτε <guiseq><gui>επεξεργασία</gui><gui>πρόσθετα</gui></guiseq>.</p></item>
<item><p>Enable <gui>Mail Notification</gui>.</p>
<note style="tip"><p>If a plugin is not available under <guiseq><gui>Edit</gui><gui>Plugins</gui></guiseq>, then please ask in a support forum of your distribution. Your distribution might have decided to disable some plugins or to ship plugins in a separate package.</p></note>
</item>
<item><p>Open the <gui style="tab">Configuration</gui> tab and set your preferred options.</p></item>
<item><p>Open the <gui style="tab">Accounts</gui> tab to select the mail accounts for which you would like to see notifications.</p></item>
</steps>

<p>See <link xref="help:gnome-help/shell-notifications" href="https://help.gnome.org/users/gnome-help/stable/shell-notifications">the GNOME Desktop Help</link> for more information.</p>

